0. Scope
--------

The Exception applies to the whole of TellerEngine: every source file,
header, build script, and data file in this repository, without
distinction between the engine core, the tooling, the software
development kit, and the components in the namespace Teller::Vanilla.

No part of TellerEngine is excluded from the Exception. Determining
whether a given part of TellerEngine is "vanilla" is not necessary in
order to know which terms apply to your work.


1. Statement of the Exception
-----------------------------

Linking TellerEngine statically or dynamically with other modules makes
a combined work based on TellerEngine. Thus, the terms and conditions of
the GPL cover the whole combination.

As a special exception, the copyright holders of TellerEngine give you
permission to combine TellerEngine with Independent Modules, as defined
in section 2, to produce an executable or other combined work,
regardless of the license terms of those Independent Modules, and to
copy and distribute the resulting work under terms of your choice,
provided that you also meet, for each Independent Module so combined,
the terms and conditions of the license of that Independent Module, and
provided that you comply with section 4 with respect to TellerEngine
itself.


2. Independent Modules
----------------------

An Independent Module is a module which is not derived from or based on
TellerEngine, other than through the interfaces TellerEngine provides
for that purpose.

For the avoidance of doubt, none of the following, by itself, prevents a
module from being an Independent Module:

  (a) including public headers of TellerEngine;

  (b) declaring, constructing, owning, or destroying instances of types
      provided by TellerEngine;

  (c) calling functions, methods, or operators provided by TellerEngine;

  (d) deriving a C++ class from a class provided by TellerEngine,
      overriding its virtual functions, and calling the base class
      implementation from an override;

  (e) specializing templates provided by TellerEngine, instantiating
      them, or providing types that satisfy concepts declared by
      TellerEngine;

  (f) reading, referring to, or copying into the module the values of
      constants, constexpr data, and descriptive tables published by
      TellerEngine;

  (g) implementing an interface declared by TellerEngine in order to
      supply data, rendering, input, audio, or timing to it;

  (h) reading or writing files, save data, or serialized state in
      formats defined or used by TellerEngine.

Paragraphs (a) through (h) are the intended use of TellerEngine as a
library. A module that does these things and no more is an Independent
Module, even though C++ makes such a module textually and structurally
dependent on TellerEngine.


3. Template, inline, and header material
----------------------------------------

Compiling an Independent Module against the headers of TellerEngine
causes template instantiations, inline functions, constexpr data, and
other header-resident material of TellerEngine to be copied into the
object code of that Independent Module. The Exception covers that copied
material: its presence in the object code of an Independent Module, and
in any work combined from it, does not cause the GPL to apply to that
Independent Module.

This section does not permit copying header-resident material of
TellerEngine into a work for a purpose other than compiling against
those headers.


4. What the Exception does not cover
------------------------------------

The Exception grants no permission to relicense TellerEngine itself.

If you modify TellerEngine, or copy any part of its source into another
work other than as described in sections 2 and 3, then the resulting
version of TellerEngine, and that other work insofar as it contains such
copied source, is a work based on TellerEngine and is governed by the
GPL in full, including the obligation to make the corresponding source
available under the GPL to the recipients of any work you convey.


5. Extending, or removing, the Exception
----------------------------------------

If you modify TellerEngine, you may extend this Exception to your
modified version, but you are not obligated to do so. If you do not wish
to extend it, you may delete this Exception statement from your version.

Deleting the Exception removes the additional permission and nothing
else. It adds no restriction to the GPL itself, and it has no effect on
the terms under which anyone received an earlier version.


6. Note on game data
--------------------

TellerEngine is source code. This repository contains no game assets,
and this document grants no rights whatsoever in any third party's
assets, data files, or copyrighted works. Nothing here changes the terms
under which you may possess or use any such material.


